1
00:00:00,050 --> 00:00:03,950
This synthetic product-behavior example shows why the refusal state matters.

2
00:00:03,950 --> 00:00:10,500
A candidate can lead the speed chart and still be rejected when task success, JSON validity, or semantic validators regress.

3
00:00:10,500 --> 00:00:14,880
Synthetic screens are clearly labelled and never presented as Arm performance evidence.

4
00:00:14,880 --> 00:00:19,320
They demonstrate the safety control: faster measurements cannot bypass correctness.

